<title>FRANCE: Sanofi gets green light for Skelid in US.</title>
<headline>Sanofi gets green light for Skelid in US.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French health and beauty products group Sanofi said on Monday it had received authorisation from the Food and Drug Administration to sell Skelid, a drug used in the treatement of a bone disease, in the United States.</p>
<p>Skelid will be put on the market by Sanofi Pharmaceuticals Inc in the coming weeks, Sanofi, a susbidiary of Elf Aquitaine, said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bone illness, known as Paget's disease, affects about three to four percent of the U.S. population over 50, Sanofi said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
